# Frontend — Next.js + TypeScript

Stack: Next.js (App Router), React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Vitest + RTL.

## Commands (pnpm only)

```bash
cd frontend
pnpm install          # deps
pnpm dev              # dev server (:3000)
pnpm test             # vitest — must pass before PR
pnpm lint             # ESLint
pnpm build            # production build — must pass before PR
```

## Conventions

- Use functional components and TypeScript strict types in `src/types/`.
- Colocate UI in `src/components/`; pages in `src/app/`.
- Fetch backend via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:8000`).
- Support light and dark mode; dark mode is default.
- Drag-and-drop UI must keep sections, modules, and contents visually distinct.
- Inline editing: use `InlineEditor` component for click-to-edit titles and content.
- Content text: first line = title, rest = body (split on save via backend `split_content_text`).
- Content types: `theory`, `exercise`, `project`, `quiz` (add new types to `schemas.py` `CONTENT_TYPES`).

## Testing

- Tests live alongside components: `Component.test.tsx`
- Use Vitest + React Testing Library (`@testing-library/react`)
- Test files: `src/components/InlineEditor.test.tsx`, `ContentTypeIcon.test.tsx`, `src/lib/content.test.ts`

## Do not

- Use `npm` or `yarn` to install or run scripts.
- Add API logic only in the frontend — backend endpoints come first.
